-- ============================================================================
-- 39 (2026-06-15): MVC2 ENGINE CAMERA (zoom/pan) — MODEL GROUNDED + REPLICA
-- REPRODUCTION AUDITED FAITHFUL. Closes the 'camera-zoom' OPEN gap flagged in
-- finding:render_replica_input_audit / project_render_input_audit.
-- feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:camera_build_disasm SET kind='code',
  ref='marvelous2 bank12 loc_8C1216C0 (M2 rebuilder) / loc_8C11FCD0 (matrix-stack init) / loc_8C122780 (M1 viewport build) / loc_8C121730 (projection-frustum build); bank03 loc_8c036804 + loc_8c03ea.. (per-frame camera-setup callers); bank11 38635 loc_8C11FCD0.',
  note='ENGINE CAMERA MODEL FULLY TRACED. (1) PROJECTION FRUSTUM M2 source: loc_8C121730 builds a perspective frustum into 0x8C2DEE20 from CONSTANT params — bank03 passes fr6=0x463b8000(=48000.0 far), fr5=0x3e99999a(=0.3), fr4=0x3faaaaab(=1.3333 aspect/fov) at BOTH call sites (loc_8c036951, loc_8c03ea..). So the raw frustum is FIXED, not per-frame. (2) THE PER-FRAME CAMERA = loc_8C1216C0 (bank12:3122): it REBUILDS M2@0x8C2D6AD8 every render frame by composing the live camera matrices off the NaomiLib matrix-stack (header @0x8C2D68E8): loc_8c120950(load *(0x8C2D690c+8)=matrix@0x8C2D69D8) -> loc_8c120540(matmul *(0x8C2D6900+8)=matrix@0x8C2D6918) -> loc_8c120660 -> loc_8c11FB70 STORES the composed XMTRX into M2@0x8C2D6AD8 -> loc_8c120900(pop). The stack descriptors @0x8C2D6900/0x8C2D690c point at the actual 4x4 float camera matrices @0x8C2D6918 and @0x8C2D69D8 (set up by loc_8C11FCD0). THESE two matrices carry the ZOOM (perspective scale) + PAN/eye (translation) + any tilt the game logic writes from the two point-chars positions each frame. (3) M1@0x8C2D6B18 = the FIXED viewport (loc_8C122780 via loc_8C122740, the negate-copy): constant [320,0,0,0; 0,-240,0,0; 0,0,-0.5,0; 320,240,0.5,1] = NDC->640x480 + screen-center translate. CONCLUSION: zoom/pan enters EXCLUSIVELY through M2 (rebuilt per-frame by loc_8c1216c0 from the camera matrices @0x8C2D6918/0x8C2D69D8); the body transform loc_8C122560 and the stage tree-walk BOTH read the already-composed M2@0x8C2D6AD8, so any zoom/pan/tilt is automatically in their XMTRX = M1.M2.';

UPSERT source:camera_live_audit SET kind='oracle',
  ref='tools/render-replica-poc/{livecap.mjs, _cam_audit.mjs} on prod wss://nobd.net/replica-live (_camcap.mcrr 600f, _camcap2.mcrr 400f) + /tmp synthetic-zoom lockstep test.',
  note='LIVE AUDIT across 1000 captured frames. (a) BODY camera math BYTE-EXACT: recomputing screen via (M1.M2).worldpos / w (the gen_transform_obj.c port the client runs) vs the engine-deposited screen +0xE0/E4 = maxDiff 4.3e-5 px, meanDiff 1.0e-5 px over 2400 char-projections. (b) The cam_mat region D(0x8C2D6AD8,0xC0) ships the FULL live M2 (incl persp scale M2[0]=2.5386/M2[5]=3.3848 and eye/pan col-3 M2[13]=-654.6/M2[14]=812.2/M2[15]=812.4) AND M1 (@+0x40) every frame. (c) LIMITATION: prod was in a FROZEN IDLE match the whole capture (chars locked at world x=+-213.3, spread 426.7; M1,M2 BIT-IDENTICAL across all 1000 frames -> 1 distinct M1, 1 distinct M2), so live zoom MOTION was not witnessable from the current prod state. (d) SYNTHETIC-ZOOM LOCKSTEP PROOF on the real captured M2: scaling M2[0]/M2[5] (the engine zoom op) by x1.6 moves a body world-pos and a stage world-vert by the IDENTICAL magnification about the viewport center (body 1.60000 == stage 1.60000); zoom-out x0.7 and pan likewise move both coherently. PROVES bodies+stage are mathematically locked to the same camera by construction.';

UPSERT finding:replica_camera_zoom_faithful SET
  statement='THE REPLICA CAMERA (zoom/pan/tilt) IS FAITHFULLY REPRODUCED — bodies AND stage track the engine camera together, by construction, with NO gap and NO fix required. GROUNDING: MVC2 puts ALL camera zoom/pan into M2@0x8C2D6AD8, which loc_8c1216c0 rebuilds every render frame by composing the live camera matrices @0x8C2D6918/0x8C2D69D8 (driven by the two point-chars positions) into the fixed projection; M1@0x8C2D6B18 is the constant viewport (source:camera_build_disasm). The replica ships M2 AND M1 in the per-frame "cam_mat" region D(0x8C2D6AD8,0xC0) (maplecast_replica_live.cpp buildTables; NOT a static prefix), captured at the STARTRENDER hook (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp:3453 onRenderFrame) AFTER loc_8c1216c0 has composed this frame`s M2 — so the snapshot is the current-frame zoomed camera. BOTH consumers read that same live M2: (1) BODIES — render_frame.wasm runs gen_transform_obj.c transform_object_122560, a faithful port of loc_8C122560 that load_mat(M1@0x8C2D6B18)*matmul(M2@0x8C2D6AD8)*ftrv(worldpos)/w from the per-frame RAM image, depositing +0xE0/E4 (so the body does NOT just read a static engine anchor — it RE-PROJECTS through the live camera, validated 4.3e-5px max vs the engine +0xE0/E4 over 1000 live frames); (2) STAGE — web/webgpu/stage-client.mjs setCamera(M1,M2) (replay.html renderStagePass reads ADDR_M1/ADDR_M2 each frame, re-projects world verts through the SAME live XMTRX=M1.M2). Because both compute screen = (M1.M2).world/w with the IDENTICAL per-frame M1,M2, they zoom/pan in exact lockstep (synthetic-zoom proof: body x-mag 1.60000 == stage x-mag 1.60000 about the viewport center; source:camera_live_audit). NO camera-angle/tilt component is lost: M2 is a full 4x4 view*projection, so any rotation/tilt the engine composes is in M2 and therefore in both XMTRX. The wire ships the matrices EVERY frame (192B, in the dynamic region set), not just the prefix. ONLY UN-WITNESSED ITEM: live zoom MOTION was not observable because prod sat in a frozen idle match the entire capture (M1/M2 bit-identical 1000 frames); the faithful-by-construction argument + byte-exact body re-projection + synthetic-zoom lockstep stand in for a moving-match capture until prod has an active match. CLOSES the camera-zoom OPEN gap (project_render_input_audit / finding:render_replica_input_audit).',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

UPSERT finding:replica_camera_zoom_live_motion_open SET
  statement='OPEN (minor, validation-only): live camera MOTION (zoom-in on close range, zoom-out on spread) has not been captured from prod because prod has been in a frozen/idle demo match (chars pinned at world x=+-213.3, M1/M2 bit-identical across 1000 captured frames). The faithful-reproduction conclusion (finding:replica_camera_zoom_faithful) rests on (1) the grounded engine model, (2) byte-exact body re-projection vs the engine-deposited +0xE0/E4, and (3) a synthetic-zoom lockstep proof on the real captured M2 — all solid. To upgrade to a live moving-match witness: capture a few hundred frames of an ACTIVE prod match (players moving toward/apart) with livecap.mjs, run tools/render-replica-poc/_cam_audit.mjs, and confirm M2[0]/M2[5] (persp zoom) and M2 col-3 (pan) VARY frame-to-frame while the body recompute stays 0px vs +0xE0/E4 — then load the same capture in replay.html and eyeball the scene zoom/pan with bodies+stage locked.',
  status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

RELATE finding:replica_camera_zoom_faithful->cites->source:camera_build_disasm;
RELATE finding:replica_camera_zoom_faithful->cites->source:camera_live_audit;
RELATE finding:replica_camera_zoom_faithful->about->finding:stage_transform_is_m1m2_CONFIRMED;
RELATE finding:replica_camera_zoom_faithful->about->finding:render_frame_positions_validated;
RELATE finding:replica_camera_zoom_live_motion_open->about->finding:replica_camera_zoom_faithful;
RELATE finding:replica_camera_zoom_live_motion_open->cites->source:camera_live_audit;
